WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.280
In the Council building,
all 27 Member States

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:12.920
meet and discuss European policy issues
and try to find a common position.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.760
We have different kinds of meetings.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:21.440
We have experts, we have ambassadors.
They meet at minister level.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.000
And finally, of course,
Heads of State and Government

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.760
as the so-called European Council.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.760
For all these meetings to be successful,
you basically need two ingredients:

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:39.640
policy advice to the presidency
and logistical support for the meetings.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:44.520
I think probably the best way
to understand how we work

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:50.920
is to see a European Council in action
from backstage.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:35.120
It's going to be a difficult
summit meeting. They always are.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:51.000
I spend a lot of time
making phone calls to capital cities.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:53.800
I attend quite a few
internal organisation meetings

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:58.960
as we work very closely together with
the Council's General Secretariat.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:04.880
I am very focused and I am focused
because much is at stake.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.640
The future of our currency,
our economy,

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:12.080
and we have to take all this
very seriously.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:19.720
It takes us five days
to prepare for a summit meeting

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:23.120
and three days to dismantle everything.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.360
We are into the Italian language now.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.880
It's 25 pages, each language version.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:42.720
My main responsibility is to prepare,
in this case, the treaty,

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:45.880
which will be signed on 2nd March.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:48.000
Today we are preparing the text.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:50.000
It should fit perfectly.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:55.560
This is a signature ceremony. You want
it to run as smoothly as possible.

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:58.040
That's the simple reason
why we're doing this.

00:02:58.520 --> 00:02:59.840
Ready to go.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:16.720
So yesterday both JuppÃ© and Hague
referred to the possibility

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:21.920
that the Arabs would table
a new resolution in New York.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:25.160
I say that we should include
in the points of his speech,

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:29.400
in the introduction, external relations,
Syria, the Arab Spring.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:37.040
There is, of course, one subject
which is still under discussion.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:41.800
So we have to wait for
today's discussions

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:45.320
because there may still be
a couple of problems around.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:59.880
We have a high-ranking visitor with
the President of the European Council.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:01.960
It's the President of Serbia.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:03.720
Things are not over.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:08.600
Serbia didn't achieve candidate status.

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:16.280
We will try to fix the problem,
probably this evening.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.480
If it is not possible,

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:21.880
we have to discuss it
at the European Council, Thursday.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:30.200
There are always problem files that
need sorting out at the last moment,

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:32.320
that's typical.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:37.520
There is positive confirmation
of the criteria being met.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.400
But the decision is not being taken.

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:46.760
I have a meeting with the Director
General of the WTO, Pascal Lamy.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:49.080
Hello.
- Herman.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:54.640
How are things? Fine?
- Fine is going a bit far.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:06.280
We'll remove those two there
and leave ten here.

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:11.040
That's the entrance but
Van Rompuy and Barroso will be here.

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:14.720
The idea is to put the flags
next to the chairs.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:22.120
A camera that gives
a wider establishing shot.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:25.200
I'm looking for the best places
to position the cameras

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:29.680
in order to have a clear shot of each
Head of State as they sign the treaty.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:33.680
Apart from the Heads, plus one,
no one will be standing up.

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:44.720
Finland.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:47.240
Germany.

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:56.120
The top line in there
is the bit about trust.

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:58.440
I'm the President's speechwriter,

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:02.880
which means I prepare his important
speeches and press conferences

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:09.360
and try to find the right words
to fit the man and the situation,

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:15.160
often in close consultation with
Mr Van Rompuy himself.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:20.760
So then I try to reorganize it
around the three key words:

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:24.440
crisis, trust and confidence.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:29.680
Enlargement will be on the agenda,

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:36.640
as well as further accession
to the Schengen area.

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:45.680
You pull that way and you pull that way.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.840
Move towards them. Lift it up,
don't let it touch the table.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.720
And put it down. Put it down.
There you are.

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:56.040
We're assembling the table for
the Heads of State and Government.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:59.800
It's a big table,
more than 11 metres long.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:04.680
We need a single tablecloth and
everyone available to help put it on.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:15.280
Is any sort of video streaming planned

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:18.840
for the signing ceremony
of the Fiscal Compact?

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:22.640
The summits are the big thing
for all the journalists here

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:26.000
and therefore it's also the big thing
for us, the spokespeople.

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:31.520
We will try to make what is agreed
on Syria available quickly.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:35.360
There are always some last minute
surprises, but also matters

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:39.200
that the President or an assistant
needs to personally smooth out

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:42.560
at the last moment before the meeting.

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:46.520
We have to wait and see.
It has to be issued this evening.

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:48.200
Everything is well prepared.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:53.320
But 27 people always have to agree
and that's the big problem.

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:57.200
There are always surprises
and you always have to improvise.

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:00.600
We are here today on the eve
of a European Council.

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:03.520
Practically, I'm responsible
for making sure that tomorrow,

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:06.320
when the Heads of State
and Government come,

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:08.400
they have all they need
to do their work.

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:12.720
It's like running a small village,
making sure that everything is there,

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:15.040
so the leaders can take
the right decisions.

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:31.800
We always have to be
ready to serve them.

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:34.720
The flowers and everything
have to be in place

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:37.720
for the arrival of
the Heads of State for the dinner.

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:48.960
This meeting is with President Barroso
and President Van Rompuy.

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:51.880
We are planning the day, basically.

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:54.640
Good morning.
- How are you? Nice to see you.

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:03.320
Let's go through the agenda
of the European Council

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:05.960
tomorrow morning.

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:10.000
If you could make it
a bit wider than that.

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:14.000
European Council is not much different,
in terms of concept,

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:16.880
from any summit that could be held
anywhere in the world.

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:19.000
The difference between
all of those and us

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.440
is that we do it
on an almost monthly basis.

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:34.960
Fiscal consolidation remains unavoidable
to keep our social model sustainable.

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:38.960
It is a very busy day.
It will end after midnight.

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:43.640
Mr President, we have good news now
concerning the candidate status.

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:47.720
They have reached an agreement
and signed the meeting protocol,

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:51.240
and we hope that this will pave the way
to a decision without discussion.

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:52.720
I think so.

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:03.440
Because everyone is right-handed.

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:33.400
They'll contact me.

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:38.160
Only the escorted vehicles
will enter Rue Froissart.

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:41.520
We have a number of participants
in this room, as you can see.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:45.120
We have the local police
for the outside perimeter.

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:48.120
We have the federal police
for escort purposes.

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:50.920
And we have the Belgian
special forces in the house,

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:54.000
for a protective mission
for a country on a higher threat level,

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:57.080
but also for interior protection.
We have people on the roofs

00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:59.840
and people on standby,
close to the main meeting room.

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:03.720
All these people together coordinate
things in case of a major event.

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:18.400
A very big day for you.

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:27.040
Have we got
any interesting relays to take?

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:33.400
I welcome you all to this meeting
of the European Council.

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:36.920
The most important thing about
interpreting is not the words,

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:40.440
it's not the language itself,
it's the message.

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:42.720
It's the spirit of
what's being put across.

00:11:46.840 --> 00:11:50.520
We have instantly to understand
what people are trying to say

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:54.440
and to convey that message
in the same tone, in the same spirit.

00:11:56.640 --> 00:11:58.880
Let's get started.

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:27.440
We're almost there,
we'll be there in 30 seconds.

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:32.400
It was tough!
- It was tough.

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:45.960
I am very honoured that you have
all decided to ask me to continue

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:50.040
as President of the European Council
for a second mandate.

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:54.560
Today we have 1,800 accredited
journalists in the press centre.

00:12:56.360 --> 00:12:59.680
There is a lot of information
flowing in this area.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:02.680
From delegations,
from institutions, etc.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:04.880
More or less informally,

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:09.160
and therefore we have to try
to always keep things in context,

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:15.240
try to give them indications about
what is being discussed, about timing.

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:24.280
With regard to a press conference
after a summit meeting,

00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:29.240
the trickiest points are often
negotiated right up to the last minute

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:34.000
and the latest news is then provided
at the press conference.

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:44.120
During this Council, we have
a wide range of issues to discuss.

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:48.480
Continuing this work for Europe
in such decisive times

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:52.960
is a privilege and a great
responsibility. Thank you.

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:13.240
There will be a day of reckoning
for this dreadful regime.

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:19.320
I'm Chief of Protocol

00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:24.320
and one of my tasks is to welcome
all high-ranking visitors

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:27.040
here on the red carpet.

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:32.160
I studied psychology
so that helps me somewhat in this job.

00:14:32.320 --> 00:14:34.920
You have to go up to them
and be cordial.

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:37.440
That means I'm a bit of
a Doctor Feelgood.

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:43.600
We're in the OB van and are filming
the arrival of the Heads of State.

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:47.880
They can arrive in any order so we don't
know who it is, it's always a surprise.

00:14:48.040 --> 00:14:50.240
Stand by, camera 5. Zoom in.

00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:55.360
... and achieve
a politically united Europe.

00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:59.480
Stand by, 1. She's going
through the door. Stand by, 6.

00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:30.360
I'm going to come up with the pool now
for the table round.

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:31.720
Let's go.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:43.560
The most difficult moment is when
the Heads of State come into the room.

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:48.800
The media wants
slightly more interesting shots,

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:50.960
which involves a lot of rushing around.

00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:54.200
That's why we're there.

00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:57.440
To stop them and
tell them to be careful.

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:04.360
It went really well.
Everyone signed, as you can see.

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:09.360
It took about 4 or 5 minutes
to go round the room, so...

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:12.720
Short and sweet.
It's a done deal.

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:22.040
What you see here are dedicated teams
of translators and assistants

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:26.320
servicing, exclusively,
the summit meeting.

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:29.800
Everyone wants to get,
as fast as possible,

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:32.880
the versions in their own language,

00:16:33.040 --> 00:16:38.120
which allows them to give
the conclusions a final check.

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:57.880
We should start in about 5 minutes.
I'll place you on hold until we start.

00:16:58.040 --> 00:16:59.360
Hello everybody.

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:02.880
What I'm doing now is a debriefing

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:05.840
for the European Union
Heads of Delegation abroad

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:09.640
because our Heads of Delegation
have questions, of course.

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:12.600
They must explain what is going on
at the European Council.

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:25.000
With this treaty
we have established balances,

00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:30.240
balances between
responsibility and solidarity.

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:33.200
See you afterwards.
Congratulations!

00:17:35.040 --> 00:17:37.600
There were some difficult subjects:

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:41.480
Serbia's application to join
the European Union.

00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:45.440
It wasn't clear at all
a few days ago

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:49.360
but we managed to iron out
all the problems.

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:53.880
So you could say
I'm a happy and satisfied man

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:57.280
after these two very intense days.

